    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35980" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνορχ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχις</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with the testicles in, uncastrated, entire,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνορχα . . μῆλ᾽ ἱερεύσειν,</span> i.e.
				<i>rams,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.147
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἔ.</span>”
				<i>entire animals,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Vict.</u>
					2.49
				</span></i>
			; also of palm-trees, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				267
			</span></i> codd. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i></div>
